                        "glosses": [
                            "Dû à un fonctionnement anormal de la nociception."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b61de78f-ec28-47fe-8d7b-d26402882474",
                                "sense_id": "4bbcd326-0023-3464-9966-0f1e9bfbf769",
                                "text": "(…) une nouvelle catégorie de douleurs vient d’être reconnue par l’association internationale d’étude spécialisée sur le sujet (IASP) : les douleurs nociplastiques."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb1a0267-c3a0-4891-aa41-d89bc5077c6b",
                        "source_entry_id": "8f66f96b-a93f-3b77-aa91-7db072f5730e",
                        "source_sense_id": "4bbcd326-0023-3464-9966-0f1e9bfbf769",
                        "target_lang_word": "nociplastic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nociplastic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f66d01ee-f6a9-36e5-9579-b1fa28d99b74",
                                        "entry_id": "bd7e7bdc-ebc8-34ad-a40e-dba488b7805b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or resulting from plasticity, of a kind analogous to neuroplasticity, in parts of the central nervous system concerned with nociception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c9542d-466a-47ba-bb63-a9980dd8c769",
                                                "sense_id": "f66d01ee-f6a9-36e5-9579-b1fa28d99b74",
                                                "text": "Patients with rheumatic conditions often have mixed pain states, with varying degrees of nociceptive, neuropathic, and nociplastic mechanisms, which exist on a continuum. When individuals with any chronic pain have a nociplastic component to their symptoms, they are less likely to respond to treatments (eg, injections, surgery, biologics, and opioids) that work better for acute or purely nociceptive pain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9745562-5f01-43e8-8149-0c953f7a5d90",
                                                "sense_id": "f66d01ee-f6a9-36e5-9579-b1fa28d99b74",
                                                "text": "Pain can be classified as nociceptive, neuropathic, or nociplastic as per the International Association for the Study of Pain [6, 7]. Fibromyalgia falls within the nociplastic classification."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca361e0d-be05-41c5-b806-ceaa186026bb",
                                                "sense_id": "f66d01ee-f6a9-36e5-9579-b1fa28d99b74",
                                                "text": "Peripheral sensitisation of nociceptive neurons can enhance or prolong the pain experience, even without sensitisation of central neurons (i.e. nociplastic or central sensitisation)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
